Author: clever-wolf-203 <clever-wolf-203@invalid>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 16:17:55 2026 +0000

    live_deploy: derive the tailscale no-read from its typed service (review 95678)
    
    The reviewer is right: NoReadOfRecord { reason: String } let a prose sentence decide whether a deploy
    proceeds. Two rules broken — source_annotations ("a String declaration whose only purpose is commentary is
    misplaced") and fail_closed ("it can be satisfied by editing the declaration while the realization still lies").
    
    Fix (the reviewer's primary path): the no-read is now DERIVED by a total match over the modeled
    TailscaleServeService, and NoReadOfRecord carries NO reason.
    - tailscale_serve_scope: the prose tailscale_serve_mapping_no_read_reason() -> String is gone; replaced by
      tailscale_serve_mapping_reads_installed_artifact(service: TailscaleServeService) -> Bool — an EXHAUSTIVE match
      (ServeCli => false). Adding a unit-backed TailscaleServeService variant makes this non-exhaustive: the build
      fails until the owner decides, so the no-read cannot survive the realization lying.
    - closure: ArtifactReadSet.NoReadOfRecord is nullary; ArtifactInventoryRow.NoReadRow carries only `located`.
      No commentary String stands between a row and Allowed.
    - adapter: TailscaleServeMapping => if the derived guard says installed-read then NotYetModeled (HALTS, never a
      silent no-read) else NoReadOfRecord. The construction path — gated on the typed derivation — is the sole
      justification.
    - new control the_tailscale_no_read_is_derived_from_the_serve_service pins both halves: the guard says ServeCli
      reads nothing installed, and the REAL adapter turns that into a NoReadRow over the srv1 roster.
    Controls PASS on base-matched seed sha256 900599bd...: the four no-read controls + inventory mapping.
    
    Node: deploy-intent-owns-artifact-closure (node://adhoc-3e6e9bfb-d59).

